<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mecca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mecca is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, the birthplace of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and the holiest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Pilgrimage to Mecca connected Muslim empires across the world, and rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a> states made the journey. Control of Mecca brought great prestige, as for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> after 1517.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mecca.jpg" alt="Mecca" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saudipics.com · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Mosque_of_Mecca1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
